# Never upload these to the edge.
#
# The asset directory is the repo root (the bundle IS the repo), so this file is
# the only thing standing between `wrangler deploy` and publishing everything in
# the working tree.
#
# ── THE INCIDENT THAT REWROTE THIS FILE ─────────────────────────────────────
#
# The first version listed `.github/` and forgot `.git/`. The first real deploy
# therefore uploaded 129 files INCLUDING THE ENTIRE REPOSITORY — .git/objects,
# .git/refs, .git/logs, .git/hooks — to a public website. A served .git
# directory lets anyone reconstruct the whole repo and its full history,
# including files deliberately deleted from the tip, which in this repo means
# the old covrd page and its fake phone numbers.
#
# It also uploaded .wrangler/tmp, wrangler's own scratch directory.
#
# The lesson, encoded rather than remembered: WATCH THE FILE COUNT. Wrangler
# prints "Read N files from the assets directory" on every deploy. This bundle
# is ~28 files. Any three-digit number means this file is not doing its job.

.git
.github
.wrangler
node_modules
tools
docs
CAPTURE.md
README.md
wrangler.toml
.assetsignore
.gitignore
